⍝ lib/group.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 18: groups: permutations, finite groups as sorted lists, subgroups, cosets, conjugacy, actions
⍝ A permutation of {0, …, n−1} is the list of its images (𝔏 ℕ): [1, 2, 0] maps 0 ↦ 1, 1 ↦ 2, 2 ↦ 0;  (p ∘ q)(i) = p(q(i)).
⍝ A finite group is the sorted list of its elements.  Inside, a point is a unary natural (0 is ⊥, k + 1 is (∷ ⊤ k)), so that an
⍝ image is read off by walking the list and two points are compared digit by digit; numerals ℕ are converted at the boundary.
⍝ ---- unary points
u′_gr ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹
u′_gr ν ≔ ((∅ᶻ ν) ⊥ (∷ ⊤ (u′_gr (⊟ᶻ ν (◀ 1)))))
u_gr ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 𝔹
u_gr ξ ≔ (u′_gr (↓ᶻ ξ))
nums_gr ∶ 𝔖 ℕ
nums_gr ≔ (iterate (ξ ↦ (⊞ ξ 1)) 0)
n′_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔖 ℕ → ℕ
n′_gr κ σ ≔ (κ (θ ι ↦ (n′_gr ι (⌄ σ))) (hd σ))
n_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → ℕ
n_gr κ ≔ (n′_gr κ nums_gr)
equ_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔹
equ_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (equ_gr ι ι′)) ⊥)) (∅ η))
cmpu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔒
cmpu_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (cmpu_gr ι ι′)) ⋗)) (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ⋖) ≖))
maxu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
maxu_gr ξ η ≔ ((cmpu_gr ξ η) η ξ ξ)
lenu_gr ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 𝔹
lenu_gr ξ ≔ (⫶ (θ ↦ ⊤) ξ)
⍝ 0, 1, …, n − 1 for a unary n
iotau′_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
iotau′_gr ν κ ≔ (ν (θ ι ↦ (∷ κ (iotau′_gr ι (∷ ⊤ κ)))) ⊥)
iotau_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
iotau_gr ν ≔ (iotau′_gr ν ⊥)
⍝ ---- permutations, inside
equp_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔹
equp_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (∧ (equ_gr θ θ′) (equp_gr ι ι′))) ⊥)) (∅ η))
cmpp_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔒
cmpp_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((cmpu_gr θ θ′) ⋖ (cmpp_gr ι ι′) ⋗)) ⋗)) (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ⋖) ≖))
⍝ the image of a point (a point beyond the list is fixed)
ap′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
ap′_gr ξ κ ο ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (κ (ζ κ′ ↦ (ap′_gr ι κ′ ο)) θ)) ο)
ap_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
ap_gr ξ κ ≔ (ap′_gr ξ κ κ)
comp_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
comp_gr ξ η ≔ (⫶ (ap_gr ξ) η)
mem_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
mem_gr ξ η ≔ (∃ₗ (equp_gr ξ) η)
⍝ pad a permutation with fixed points to n points
pad′_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
pad′_gr ν ξ κ ≔ (ν (θ ν′ ↦ (ξ (ζ ι ↦ (∷ ζ (pad′_gr ν′ ι (∷ ⊤ κ)))) (∷ κ (pad′_gr ν′ ⊥ (∷ ⊤ κ))))) ⊥)
pad_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
pad_gr ν ξ ≔ (pad′_gr ν ξ ⊥)
degs_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 𝔹
degs_gr ξ ≔ (foldl (ζ θ ↦ (maxu_gr ζ (lenu_gr θ))) ⊥ ξ)
⍝ ---- merge sort with a three-way comparison; usort_gr drops duplicates, ksort_gr keeps them (not stable: equal keys may be reordered)
split_gr ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔓 (𝔏 α) (𝔏 α)
split_gr ξ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ ((σ ↦ (⊗ (∷ θ (▶ σ)) (◀ σ))) (split_gr ι))) (⊗ ⊥ ⊥))
umerge_gr ∶ (α → α → 𝔒) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
umerge_gr ϰ ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((ϰ θ θ′) (∷ θ (umerge_gr ϰ ι η)) (∷ θ (umerge_gr ϰ ι ι′)) (∷ θ′ (umerge_gr ϰ ξ ι′)))) ξ)) η)
usort_gr ∶ (α → α → 𝔒) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
usort_gr ϰ ξ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (ι (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((σ ↦ (umerge_gr ϰ (usort_gr ϰ (◀ σ)) (usort_gr ϰ (▶ σ)))) (split_gr ξ))) (∷ θ ⊥))) ⊥)
kmerge_gr ∶ (α → α → 𝔒) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
kmerge_gr ϰ ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((ϰ θ θ′) (∷ θ (kmerge_gr ϰ ι η)) (∷ θ (kmerge_gr ϰ ι η)) (∷ θ′ (kmerge_gr ϰ ξ ι′)))) ξ)) η)
ksort_gr ∶ (α → α → 𝔒) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
ksort_gr ϰ ξ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (ι (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((σ ↦ (kmerge_gr ϰ (ksort_gr ϰ (◀ σ)) (ksort_gr ϰ (▶ σ)))) (split_gr ξ))) (∷ θ ⊥))) ⊥)
⍝ ---- boundary: ℕ permutations and groups in and out
⍝ min(x, n) as a unary point, n given as a list of length n (so an out-of-range entry costs O(n), never O(x))
uc′_gr ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 𝔹
uc′_gr ν ζ ≔ ((∅ᶻ ν) ⊥ (ζ (θ ι ↦ (∷ ⊤ (uc′_gr (⊟ᶻ ν (◀ 1)) ι))) ⊥))
uc_gr ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 𝔹
uc_gr ξ ζ ≔ (uc′_gr (↓ᶻ ξ) ζ)
inp_gr ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
inp_gr ξ ≔ (⫶ (θ ↦ (uc_gr θ ξ)) ξ)
outp_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 ℕ
outp_gr ξ ≔ (⫶ n_gr ξ)
⍝ a list of permutations, padded to a common degree (not sorted)
inl_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
inl_gr ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ (⫶ (pad_gr (degs_gr σ)) σ)) (⫶ inp_gr ξ))
⍝ a group: padded, sorted, without repetitions
ing_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
ing_gr ξ ≔ (usort_gr cmpp_gr (inl_gr ξ))
outg_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
outg_gr ξ ≔ (⫶ outp_gr ξ)
⍝ ---- sorted sets (by a three-way comparison): difference, subset, equality
diff_gr ∶ (α → α → 𝔒) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
diff_gr ϰ ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((ϰ θ θ′) (∷ θ (diff_gr ϰ ι η)) (diff_gr ϰ ι ι′) (diff_gr ϰ ξ ι′))) ξ)) ⊥)
subs_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
subs_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((cmpp_gr θ θ′) ⊥ (subs_gr ι ι′) (subs_gr ξ ι′))) ⊥)) ⊤)
eqs_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
eqs_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (∧ (equp_gr θ θ′) (eqs_gr ι ι′))) ⊥)) (∅ η))
cmps_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔒
cmps_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((cmpp_gr θ θ′) ⋖ (cmps_gr ι ι′) ⋗)) ⋗)) (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ ⋖) ≖))
⍝ groups ordered by their order, then lexicographically
cmpo_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔒
cmpo_gr ξ η ≔ ((cmpu_gr (lenu_gr ξ) (lenu_gr η)) ⋖ (cmps_gr ξ η) ⋗)
⍝ ---- closure: the group generated by a list of permutations of one degree, breadth first; the products of the newest layer
⍝ with the generators, sorted, minus what is known, form the next layer (so the result comes out sorted)
gen′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
gen′_gr ϰ σ φ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((∅ ν) σ (gen′_gr ϰ (umerge_gr cmpp_gr σ ν) ν))) (diff_gr cmpp_gr (usort_gr cmpp_gr (concat (⫶ (χ ↦ (⫶ (comp_gr χ) ϰ)) φ))) σ))
gen_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
gen_gr ϰ ≔ ((ε ↦ (gen′_gr ϰ (∷ ε ⊥) (∷ ε ⊥))) (iotau_gr (degs_gr ϰ)))
⍝ the same search, returning the elements layer after layer (breadth-first order, the identity first)
bfsn′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
bfsn′_gr ϰ σ φ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((∅ ν) ⊥ (⧺ ν (bfsn′_gr ϰ (umerge_gr cmpp_gr σ ν) ν)))) (diff_gr cmpp_gr (usort_gr cmpp_gr (concat (⫶ (χ ↦ (⫶ (comp_gr χ) ϰ)) φ))) σ))
bfsn_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
bfsn_gr ϰ ε ≔ (∷ ε (bfsn′_gr ϰ (∷ ε ⊥) (∷ ε ⊥)))
⍝ ---- more inside helpers: inverse, cycles, unary arithmetic, orders
⍝ the position of a point in a list (the point itself when it does not occur)
idx′_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
idx′_gr κ ξ ρ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ ((equ_gr θ κ) ρ (idx′_gr κ ι (∷ ⊤ ρ)))) κ)
inv_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
inv_gr ξ ≔ (⫶ (κ ↦ (idx′_gr κ ξ ⊥)) (iotau_gr (lenu_gr ξ)))
⍝ ζ ξ ζ⁻¹, given ζ⁻¹ = ζ′
conj_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
conj_gr ξ ζ ζ′ ≔ (comp_gr ζ (comp_gr ξ ζ′))
geu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔹
geu_gr ξ η ≔ ((cmpu_gr ξ η) ⊥ ⊤ ⊤)
⍝ the cycle of κ: κ, p(κ), p(p(κ)), … — at most n points (the fuel φ), so that a list that is not a permutation still terminates
cyc′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
cyc′_gr ξ κ μ φ ≔ (φ (θ φ′ ↦ ((equ_gr μ κ) ⊥ (∷ μ (cyc′_gr ξ κ (ap_gr ξ μ) φ′)))) ⊥)
cyc_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
cyc_gr ξ κ ≔ (∷ κ (cyc′_gr ξ κ (ap_gr ξ κ) ξ))
⍝ all cycles, fixed points included, each from its least point, in increasing order of that point
cycs_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
cycs_gr ξ ≔ (⫶ (cyc_gr ξ) (filter (κ ↦ (¬ (∅ (clen_gr ξ κ)))) (iotau_gr (lenu_gr ξ))))
⍝ the length of the cycle of κ if κ is its least point, else 0: the walk stops at the first smaller point (fuel n as above)
clen′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 𝔹
clen′_gr ξ κ μ λ φ ≔ (φ (θ φ′ ↦ ((cmpu_gr μ κ) ⊥ λ (clen′_gr ξ κ (ap_gr ξ μ) (∷ ⊤ λ) φ′))) ⊥)
clen_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
clen_gr ξ κ ≔ (clen′_gr ξ κ (ap_gr ξ κ) (∷ ⊤ ⊥) ξ)
⍝ the lengths of all cycles (fixed points included), one per cycle, in order of their least point
lens_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
lens_gr ξ ≔ (filter (ζ ↦ (¬ (∅ ζ))) (⫶ (clen_gr ξ) (iotau_gr (lenu_gr ξ))))
⍝ unary arithmetic: μ − β handed to κ when β ≤ μ (else φ), divisibility, quotient, product, lcm
subu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → (𝔏 𝔹 → α) → α → α
subu_gr μ ν κ φ ≔ (ν (θ ν′ ↦ (μ (ζ μ′ ↦ (subu_gr μ′ ν′ κ φ)) φ)) (κ μ))
dvdu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔹
dvdu_gr μ ν ≔ ((∅ μ) ⊤ ((∅ ν) ⊥ (subu_gr μ ν (ρ ↦ (dvdu_gr ρ ν)) ⊥)))
divu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
divu_gr μ ν ≔ ((∅ ν) ⊥ (subu_gr μ ν (ρ ↦ (∷ ⊤ (divu_gr ρ ν))) ⊥))
mulu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
mulu_gr μ ν ≔ (concat (⫶ (θ ↦ μ) ν))
lcmu′_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
lcmu′_gr μ ν ρ ≔ ((dvdu_gr ρ ν) ρ (lcmu′_gr μ ν (⧺ ρ μ)))
lcmu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
lcmu_gr μ ν ≔ ((∅ μ) ν ((∅ ν) μ (lcmu′_gr μ ν μ)))
⍝ the order of a permutation: the lcm of its cycle lengths (unary)
ordu_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹
ordu_gr ξ ≔ (foldl lcmu_gr (∷ ⊤ ⊥) (lens_gr ξ))
⍝ odd permutation ⇔ an odd number of cycles of even length
evl_gr ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔹
evl_gr ξ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (¬ (evl_gr ι))) ⊤)
odd_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔹
odd_gr ξ ≔ (foldl (ρ ζ ↦ (⊻ ρ (evl_gr ζ))) ⊥ (lens_gr ξ))
⍝ x^ν for a natural ν given by its digits (square and multiply: odd ⇔ last digit 1)
pw_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔇 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
pw_gr ξ ν ≔ ((∅ᶻ ν) (iotau_gr (lenu_gr ξ)) ((⌃ ν) (comp_gr ξ (pw_gr ξ (⊟ᶻ ν (◀ 1)))) ((θ ↦ (comp_gr θ θ)) (pw_gr ξ (⊡ (½ᶻ ν))))))
⍝ two lists of permutations padded to a common degree, each sorted without repetitions
ing2_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))) (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))
ing2_gr ξ η ≔ ((σ τ ↦ ((ν ↦ (⊗ (usort_gr cmpp_gr (⫶ (pad_gr ν) σ)) (usort_gr cmpp_gr (⫶ (pad_gr ν) τ)))) (maxu_gr (degs_gr σ) (degs_gr τ)))) (⫶ inp_gr ξ) (⫶ inp_gr η))
⍝ ---- public: permutations
pid ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the identity permutation of n points [0, 1, …, n − 1]
pid ξ ≔ (⍳ ξ)
isperm ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔹      ⍝ is the list a permutation of {0, …, n − 1} (n its length)?
isperm ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ (equp_gr (usort_gr cmpu_gr σ) (iotau_gr (lenu_gr σ)))) (inp_gr ξ))
pcompose ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ composition (p ∘ q)(i) = p(q(i)); the shorter permutation is extended by fixed points
pcompose ξ η ≔ ((σ ↦ (outp_gr (comp_gr (hd σ) (hd (⌄ σ))))) (inl_gr (∷ ξ (∷ η ⊥))))
pinverse ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the inverse permutation p⁻¹
pinverse ξ ≔ (outp_gr (inv_gr (inp_gr ξ)))
papply ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the image p(i) of a point (a point beyond the list is fixed)
papply ξ κ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((ν ↦ ((equ_gr ν (lenu_gr σ)) κ (n_gr (ap_gr σ ν)))) (uc_gr κ σ))) (inp_gr ξ))
porder ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the order of a permutation: the lcm of its cycle lengths
porder ξ ≔ (n_gr (ordu_gr (inp_gr ξ)))
ppow ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the power pᵏ, k ∈ ℤ (k is reduced modulo the order, then square and multiply)
ppow ξ κ ≔ (outp_gr (pw_gr (inp_gr ξ) (↓ᶻ (mod κ (porder ξ)))))
pcycles ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the cycles of length ≥ 2, each starting at its least point, sorted by that point
pcycles ξ ≔ (⫶ outp_gr (filter (ζ ↦ (¬ (∅ (⌄ ζ)))) (cycs_gr (inp_gr ξ))))
⍝ one cycle (a₀ a₁ … a_k) = (a₀ a_k)…(a₀ a₂)(a₀ a₁), applied to a point: a product of transpositions, so any list of points is a permutation
swap_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
swap_gr μ ν κ ≔ ((equ_gr κ μ) ν ((equ_gr κ ν) μ κ))
cycap_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
cycap_gr ζ κ ≔ (ζ (θ ι ↦ (foldl (μ ν ↦ (swap_gr θ ν μ)) κ ι)) κ)
fromcycles ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the permutation of max(n, 1 + largest point) points with the given cycles; cycles that overlap are composed, the first one last applied: c₁ ∘ c₂ ∘ …
fromcycles ξ η ≔ ((ζ ↦ (outp_gr (⫶ (κ ↦ (foldr cycap_gr κ ζ)) (iotau_gr (foldl (ρ θ ↦ (maxu_gr ρ (∷ ⊤ θ))) (u_gr ξ) (concat ζ)))))) (⫶ (⫶ u_gr) η))
psign ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → ℤ      ⍝ the sign of a permutation: 1 (even) or −1 (odd)
psign ξ ≔ ((odd_gr (inp_gr ξ)) 11101 1)
iseven ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔹      ⍝ is the permutation even (a product of an even number of transpositions)?
iseven ξ ≔ (¬ (odd_gr (inp_gr ξ)))
cycletype ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the cycle type: the lengths of all cycles, fixed points included, in decreasing order (a partition of n)
cycletype ξ ≔ (⫶ n_gr (ksort_gr (μ ν ↦ (cmpu_gr ν μ)) (lens_gr (inp_gr ξ))))
pconj ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the conjugate q p q⁻¹ of p by q
pconj ξ η ≔ ((σ ↦ ((ζ ↦ (outp_gr (conj_gr (hd σ) ζ (inv_gr ζ)))) (hd (⌄ σ)))) (inl_gr (∷ ξ (∷ η ⊥))))
⍝ ---- public: groups
generate ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the group generated by a list of permutations: all its elements, sorted lexicographically (closure by search)
generate ξ ≔ (outg_gr (gen_gr (inl_gr ξ)))
⍝ all permutations of a sorted list of points, in lexicographic order
perms_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
perms_gr ξ ≔ ((∅ ξ) (∷ ⊥ ⊥) (concat (⫶ (θ ↦ (⫶ (∷ θ) (perms_gr (filter (ζ ↦ (¬ (equ_gr ζ θ))) ξ)))) ξ)))
symgroup ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the symmetric group Sₙ: all n! permutations of n points, sorted (S₀ = [[]])
symgroup ξ ≔ (outg_gr (perms_gr (iotau_gr (u_gr ξ))))
altgroup ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the alternating group Aₙ: the even permutations of n points, sorted
altgroup ξ ≔ (outg_gr (filter (θ ↦ (¬ (odd_gr θ))) (perms_gr (iotau_gr (u_gr ξ)))))
dropu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
dropu_gr κ ξ ≔ (κ (θ ι ↦ (dropu_gr ι (⌄ ξ))) ξ)
takeu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
takeu_gr κ ξ ≔ (κ (θ ι ↦ (ξ (ζ ω ↦ (∷ ζ (takeu_gr ι ω))) ⊥)) ⊥)
⍝ the rotations i ↦ i + k and the reflections i ↦ k − i (mod n) of n points
rots_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
rots_gr ν ≔ ((ι′ ↦ (⫶ (κ ↦ (⧺ (dropu_gr κ ι′) (takeu_gr κ ι′))) ι′)) (iotau_gr ν))
refls_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
refls_gr ν ≔ ((ι′ ↦ (⫶ (κ ↦ (⧺ (reverse (takeu_gr (∷ ⊤ κ) ι′)) (reverse (dropu_gr (∷ ⊤ κ) ι′)))) ι′)) (iotau_gr ν))
⍝ the cyclic group and the symmetries of the n-gon acting on its n vertices (the image of the action: for n ≤ 2 of order < 2n)
cycz_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
cycz_gr ν ≔ ((∅ ν) (∷ ⊥ ⊥) (rots_gr ν))
dih_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
dih_gr ν ≔ ((∅ ν) (∷ ⊥ ⊥) (usort_gr cmpp_gr (⧺ (rots_gr ν) (refls_gr ν))))
cyclicgroup ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the cyclic group Cₙ: the n rotations of n points, sorted (C₀ is the trivial group [[]])
cyclicgroup ξ ≔ (outg_gr (cycz_gr (u_gr ξ)))
kleingroup ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the Klein four-group V₄ = {id, (0 1)(2 3), (0 2)(1 3), (0 3)(1 2)} on 4 points
kleingroup ≔ (∷ (∷ 0 (∷ 1 (∷ 1100 (∷ 1101 ⊥)))) (∷ (∷ 1 (∷ 0 (∷ 1101 (∷ 1100 ⊥)))) (∷ (∷ 1100 (∷ 1101 (∷ 0 (∷ 1 ⊥)))) (∷ (∷ 1101 (∷ 1100 (∷ 1 (∷ 0 ⊥)))) ⊥))))
dihedralgroup ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the dihedral group of order 2n: the symmetries of the n-gon on its n vertices (n ≥ 3); D₁ = C₂ on 2 points, D₂ = V₄ on 4 points, D₀ = [[]]
dihedralgroup ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((∅ ν) (∷ ⊥ ⊥) ((∅ (⌄ ν)) (symgroup 1100) ((∅ (⌄ (⌄ ν))) kleingroup (outg_gr (dih_gr ν)))))) (u_gr ξ))
⍝ ---- Cayley's theorem: a group given by its elements and its operation, as permutations of the positions of its elements
⍝ dd′_gr: the list without repetitions (first occurrences, order kept); fnde_gr: (found, position)
dd′_gr ∶ (α → α → 𝔹) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
dd′_gr ε ξ σ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ ((∃ₗ (ε θ) σ) (dd′_gr ε ι σ) (∷ θ (dd′_gr ε ι (∷ θ σ))))) ⊥)
fnde_gr ∶ (α → α → 𝔹) → α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔓 𝔹 (𝔏 𝔹)
fnde_gr ε ξ η ρ ≔ (η (θ ι ↦ ((ε ξ θ) (⊗ ⊤ ρ) (fnde_gr ε ξ ι (∷ ⊤ ρ)))) (⊗ ⊥ ρ))
dstu_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔹
dstu_gr ξ ≔ (equ_gr (lenu_gr (usort_gr cmpu_gr ξ)) (lenu_gr ξ))
⍝ L_a ∘ L_b = L_(a·b) for all a, b (associativity); with injective, bijective L the elements then form a group isomorphic to {L_a}
assoc_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
assoc_gr σ ≔ (∀ₗ (θ ↦ (∀ₗ (τ ↦ (equp_gr (comp_gr θ (◀ τ)) (nthu_gr σ (nthu_gr θ (▶ τ))))) (wix_gr σ))) σ)
reg′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔓 𝔹 (𝔏 𝔹))) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
reg′_gr ρ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((∧ (∧ (∀ₗ (τ ↦ (∧ (∀ₗ (υ ↦ (◀ υ)) τ) (dstu_gr (⫶ (υ ↦ (▶ υ)) τ)))) ρ) (equ_gr (lenu_gr (usort_gr cmpp_gr σ)) (lenu_gr σ))) (assoc_gr σ)) (usort_gr cmpp_gr σ) ⊥)) (⫶ (τ ↦ (⫶ (υ ↦ (▶ υ)) τ)) ρ))
reg_gr ∶ (α → α → 𝔹) → 𝔏 α → (α → α → α) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
reg_gr ε ξ ω ≔ ((σ ↦ (outg_gr (reg′_gr (⫶ (θ ↦ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (fnde_gr ε (ω θ ζ) σ ⊥)) σ)) σ)))) (dd′_gr ε ξ ⊥))
regular ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → (ℕ → ℕ → ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ Cayley's theorem: the group of the left multiplications x ↦ g·x, as permutations of the positions of the (distinct) elements; [] unless the elements form a group under the operation (closed, every x ↦ g·x a bijection, g ↦ (x ↦ g·x) injective, associative; O(n⁴) checks, small n)
regular ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → (ℤ → ℤ → ℤ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
regular ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → (ℚ → ℚ → ℚ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
regular ∶ 𝔏 ℤ[i] → (ℤ[i] → ℤ[i] → ℤ[i]) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
regular ∶ 𝔏 ℚ[i] → (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
regular ξ ω ≔ (reg_gr ≐ ξ ω)
regular𝔻 ∶ 𝔏 𝔻 → (𝔻 → 𝔻 → 𝔻) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ Cayley's theorem for elements of the Cayley–Dickson tower (e.g. the quaternion units under ⊠𝔻)
regular𝔻 ξ ω ≔ (reg_gr (≐ᵀ 𝔸ℚ[i] ≐) ξ ω)
regularᵖ ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → (𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ Cayley's theorem for elements that are lists (e.g. permutations under pcompose; compared entry by entry)
regularᵖ ξ ω ≔ (reg_gr (eqlist ≐) ξ ω)
regularᵐ ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ[i])) → (𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ[i]) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ[i]) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ[i])) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ Cayley's theorem for matrices (e.g. under mmul)
regularᵐ ξ ω ≔ (reg_gr (eqlist (eqlist ≐)) ξ ω)
quaterniongroup ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the quaternion group Q₈ = {±1, ±i, ±j, ±k} of the Cayley–Dickson tower, by Cayley's theorem on 8 points (1, −1, i, −i, j, −j, k, −k)
quaterniongroup ≔ (regular𝔻 (∷ (↑ 1) (∷ (↑ 11101) (∷ (↑ 11) (∷ (↑ 111) (∷ 𝕛 (∷ (⊖𝔻 𝕛) (∷ 𝕜 (∷ (⊖𝔻 𝕜) ⊥)))))))) ⊠𝔻)
⍝ ---- inside helpers for groups (sorted lists of permutations of one degree)
⍝ a permutation; a group; H a subgroup of G.  Closure is tested with a few generators: elements of G outside the subgroup K
⍝ generated so far are added until G ⊆ K; then G is a group iff |K| = |G| (the closure stops as soon as it outgrows G)
permi_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔹
permi_gr ξ ≔ (equp_gr (usort_gr cmpu_gr ξ) (iotau_gr (lenu_gr ξ)))
bgen′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
bgen′_gr ϰ β σ φ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((∅ ν) σ ((τ ↦ ((geu_gr β (lenu_gr τ)) (bgen′_gr ϰ β τ ν) τ)) (umerge_gr cmpp_gr σ ν)))) (diff_gr cmpp_gr (usort_gr cmpp_gr (concat (⫶ (χ ↦ (⫶ (comp_gr χ) ϰ)) φ))) σ))
grp′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
grp′_gr ξ σ κ ≔ ((ρ ↦ ((∅ ρ) (equ_gr (lenu_gr κ) (lenu_gr ξ)) ((φ ↦ ((τ ↦ ((geu_gr (lenu_gr ξ) (lenu_gr τ)) (grp′_gr ξ φ τ) ⊥)) ((ε ↦ (bgen′_gr φ (lenu_gr ξ) (∷ ε ⊥) (∷ ε ⊥))) (iotau_gr (degs_gr ξ))))) (∷ (hd ρ) σ)))) (diff_gr cmpp_gr ξ κ))
clos_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
clos_gr ξ ≔ (grp′_gr ξ ⊥ (∷ (iotau_gr (degs_gr ξ)) ⊥))
grp_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
grp_gr ξ ≔ (∧ (¬ (∅ ξ)) (∧ (∀ₗ permi_gr ξ) (clos_gr ξ)))
sgp_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
sgp_gr η ξ ≔ (∧ (¬ (∅ η)) (∧ (subs_gr η ξ) (clos_gr η)))
⍝ the elements paired with their inverses
invs_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))
invs_gr ξ ≔ (⫶ (θ ↦ (⊗ θ (inv_gr θ))) ξ)
⍝ the centre; the subgroup generated by the commutators a b a⁻¹ b⁻¹; the normalizer of a set η in ξ
cent_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
cent_gr ξ ≔ (filter (θ ↦ (∀ₗ (ζ ↦ (equp_gr (comp_gr θ ζ) (comp_gr ζ θ))) ξ)) ξ)
comm_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
comm_gr ξ ≔ ((ω ↦ (gen_gr (usort_gr cmpp_gr (concat (⫶ (τ ↦ (⫶ (υ ↦ (comp_gr (comp_gr (◀ τ) (◀ υ)) (comp_gr (▶ τ) (▶ υ)))) ω)) ω))))) (invs_gr ξ))
norm_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
norm_gr η ξ ≔ (filter (θ ↦ ((ζ ↦ (eqs_gr (usort_gr cmpp_gr (⫶ (υ ↦ (conj_gr υ θ ζ)) η)) η)) (inv_gr θ))) ξ)
abel_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
abel_gr ξ ≔ (∀ₗ (θ ↦ (∀ₗ (ζ ↦ (equp_gr (comp_gr θ ζ) (comp_gr ζ θ))) ξ)) ξ)
cycl_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
cycl_gr ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (∃ₗ (θ ↦ (equ_gr (ordu_gr θ) ν)) ξ)) (lenu_gr ξ))
⍝ the derived series G ⊇ G′ ⊇ G″ … reaches the trivial group (solvable) or stops (G⁽ᵏ⁺¹⁾ = G⁽ᵏ⁾ ≠ 1)
solv_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
solv_gr ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((∅ (⌄ σ)) ⊤ ((equ_gr (lenu_gr σ) (lenu_gr ξ)) ⊥ (solv_gr σ)))) (comm_gr ξ))
⍝ runs of a sorted list of unary numbers: (value, count)
rle′_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹))
rle′_gr θ κ ξ ≔ (ξ (θ′ ι ↦ ((equ_gr θ θ′) (rle′_gr θ (∷ ⊤ κ) ι) (∷ (⊗ θ κ) (rle′_gr θ′ (∷ ⊤ ⊥) ι)))) (∷ (⊗ θ κ) ⊥))
rle_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹))
rle_gr ξ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (rle′_gr θ (∷ ⊤ ⊥) ι)) ⊥)
⍝ the element-order statistics: (order, count), by increasing order
eord_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹))
eord_gr ξ ≔ (rle_gr (ksort_gr cmpu_gr (⫶ ordu_gr ξ)))
eqo_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
eqo_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (∧ (∧ (equ_gr (◀ θ) (◀ θ′)) (equ_gr (▶ θ) (▶ θ′))) (eqo_gr ι ι′))) ⊥)) (∅ η))
⍝ the orbit of a point under the group generated by ϰ (closure of a set of points); all orbits on 0 … n − 1
orb′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
orb′_gr ϰ σ ≔ ((τ ↦ ((equ_gr (lenu_gr τ) (lenu_gr σ)) σ (orb′_gr ϰ τ))) (usort_gr cmpu_gr (⧺ σ (concat (⫶ (κ ↦ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (ap_gr ζ κ)) ϰ)) σ)))))
orb_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
orb_gr ϰ κ ≔ (orb′_gr ϰ (∷ κ ⊥))
orbs′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
orbs′_gr ϰ ρ ≔ (ρ (θ ι ↦ ((σ ↦ (∷ σ (orbs′_gr ϰ (filter (κ ↦ (¬ (∃ₗ (equ_gr κ) σ))) ρ)))) (orb_gr ϰ θ))) ⊥)
orbs_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
orbs_gr ϰ ≔ (orbs′_gr ϰ (iotau_gr (degs_gr ϰ)))
⍝ the fixed points of a permutation (unary count); Burnside: the number of orbits is the mean number of fixed points
fix′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
fix′_gr ξ κ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ ((equ_gr θ κ) (∷ ⊤ (fix′_gr ι (∷ ⊤ κ))) (fix′_gr ι (∷ ⊤ κ)))) ⊥)
burn_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 𝔹
burn_gr ξ ≔ (divu_gr (concat (⫶ (θ ↦ (fix′_gr θ ⊥)) ξ)) (lenu_gr ξ))
⍝ cosets ϰ(θ, H) of H covering ρ, each sorted, in order of their least element; conjugacy classes likewise
cos′_gr ∶ (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))
cos′_gr ϰ η ρ ≔ (ρ (θ ι ↦ ((σ ↦ (∷ σ (cos′_gr ϰ η (diff_gr cmpp_gr ρ σ)))) (usort_gr cmpp_gr (⫶ (ϰ θ) η)))) ⊥)
ccl′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))
ccl′_gr ω ρ ≔ (ρ (θ ι ↦ ((σ ↦ (∷ σ (ccl′_gr ω (diff_gr cmpp_gr ρ σ)))) (usort_gr cmpp_gr (⫶ (τ ↦ (conj_gr θ (◀ τ) (▶ τ))) ω)))) ⊥)
ccl_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))
ccl_gr ξ ≔ (ccl′_gr (invs_gr ξ) ξ)
⍝ a list with unary positions (x, 0), (y, 1), …; the element at a unary position; the position of a permutation (its length if absent)
wix′_gr ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔓 α (𝔏 𝔹))
wix′_gr ξ κ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (∷ (⊗ θ κ) (wix′_gr ι (∷ ⊤ κ)))) ⊥)
wix_gr ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 (𝔓 α (𝔏 𝔹))
wix_gr ξ ≔ (wix′_gr ξ ⊥)
nthu_gr ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 𝔹 → α
nthu_gr ξ κ ≔ (κ (θ ι ↦ (nthu_gr (⌄ ξ) ι)) (hd ξ))
pos′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
pos′_gr ξ η κ ≔ (η (θ ι ↦ ((equp_gr θ ξ) κ (pos′_gr ξ ι (∷ ⊤ κ)))) κ)
⍝ a row of the Cayley table: (θ·G = G, the positions of θ∘g for g ∈ G) — two stable sorts, no search
crow_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔓 𝔹 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
crow_gr ξ θ ≔ ((σ ↦ (⊗ (eqs_gr (⫶ ◀ σ) ξ) (⫶ ▶ (ksort_gr (μ ν ↦ (cmpu_gr (◀ μ) (◀ ν))) (wix_gr (⫶ ▶ σ)))))) (ksort_gr (μ ν ↦ (cmpp_gr (◀ μ) (◀ ν))) (wix_gr (⫶ (comp_gr θ) ξ))))
⍝ the direct product on disjoint points: (g, h) acts as g on 0 … n − 1 and as h shifted by n
dprod_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
dprod_gr ξ η ≔ ((ν ↦ (concat (⫶ (θ ↦ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⧺ θ (⫶ (⧺ ν) ζ))) η)) ξ))) (degs_gr ξ))
⍝ ---- Sylow subgroups: grow a p-subgroup P by an element x ∈ N(P) ∖ P with xᵖ ∈ P until |P| is the p-part of |G|
powu_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)
powu_gr ξ κ ≔ (foldl (ρ θ ↦ (comp_gr ρ ξ)) (iotau_gr (lenu_gr ξ)) κ)
ppw_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
ppw_gr ν κ ≔ ((∧ (¬ (∅ ν)) (dvdu_gr ν κ)) (mulu_gr κ (ppw_gr (divu_gr ν κ) κ)) (∷ ⊤ ⊥))
primeu_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔹
primeu_gr κ ≔ (∧ (geu_gr κ (∷ ⊤ (∷ ⊤ ⊥))) (∀ₗ (μ ↦ (∨ (geu_gr (∷ ⊤ ⊥) μ) (¬ (dvdu_gr κ μ)))) (iotau_gr κ)))
syl′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
syl′_gr ξ κ τ ρ ≔ ((equ_gr (lenu_gr ρ) τ) ρ (syl′_gr ξ κ τ (gen_gr (∷ (hd (filter (θ ↦ (mem_gr (powu_gr θ κ) ρ)) (diff_gr cmpp_gr (norm_gr ρ ξ) ρ))) ρ))))
syl_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
syl_gr ξ κ ≔ (syl′_gr ξ κ (ppw_gr (lenu_gr ξ) κ) (∷ (iotau_gr (degs_gr ξ)) ⊥))
⍝ ---- all subgroups: the cyclic ones, then joins ⟨H, c⟩ with every cyclic c until nothing new (subgroups carried with generators)
cysub_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))) (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))))
cysub_gr ξ ≔ (usort_gr (μ ν ↦ (cmps_gr (◀ μ) (◀ ν))) (⫶ (θ ↦ (⊗ (gen_gr (∷ θ ⊥)) (∷ θ ⊥))) ξ))
sgr′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))) (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))) (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))) (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))) (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))))
sgr′_gr ψ χ ω ≔ ((ϰ ↦ ((ν ↦ ((∅ ν) χ (sgr′_gr ψ (umerge_gr ϰ χ ν) ν))) (diff_gr ϰ (usort_gr ϰ (concat (⫶ (τ ↦ (⫶ (υ ↦ ((ζ ↦ (⊗ (gen_gr ζ) ζ)) (⧺ (▶ τ) (▶ υ)))) (filter (υ ↦ (¬ (∨ (subs_gr (◀ υ) (◀ τ)) (subs_gr (◀ τ) (◀ υ))))) ψ))) ω))) χ))) (μ ν ↦ (cmps_gr (◀ μ) (◀ ν))))
sgrs_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))
sgrs_gr ξ ≔ ((ψ ↦ (⫶ ◀ (sgr′_gr ψ ψ ψ))) (cysub_gr ξ))
⍝ ---- a generating list (greedy: an element of largest order outside the subgroup generated so far) and the Cayley graph
⍝ for it: the elements in breadth-first order, every edge (y, s, y∘s) as unary positions, and for every element but the
⍝ identity its first incoming edge (a spanning tree: the parent comes earlier)
ggen′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
ggen′_gr ξ σ κ ≔ ((ρ ↦ ((∅ ρ) σ ((φ ↦ (ggen′_gr ξ φ (gen_gr φ))) (⧺ σ (∷ (hd ρ) ⊥))))) (filter (θ ↦ (¬ (mem_gr θ κ))) ξ))
ggen_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
ggen_gr ξ ≔ (ggen′_gr (⫶ ▶ (ksort_gr (μ ν ↦ (cmpu_gr (◀ ν) (◀ μ))) (⫶ (θ ↦ (⊗ (ordu_gr θ) θ)) ξ))) ⊥ (∷ (iotau_gr (degs_gr ξ)) ⊥))
edg_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹)))
edg_gr ν ς ≔ (concat (⫶ (τ ↦ (⫶ (υ ↦ (⊗ (▶ τ) (⊗ (▶ υ) (pos′_gr (comp_gr (◀ τ) (◀ υ)) ν ⊥)))) (wix_gr ς))) (wix_gr ν)))
tre_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹))) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹)))
tre_gr ν ε ≔ (⫶ (κ ↦ (hd (filter (τ ↦ (equ_gr (▶ (▶ τ)) κ)) ε))) (⌄ (iotau_gr (lenu_gr ν))))
⍝ the values along the tree: the root gets ρ's single entry, a child ϖ(value of its parent, its generator's position)
tval_gr ∶ (α → 𝔏 𝔹 → α) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹))) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
tval_gr ϰ ϑ ρ ≔ (ϑ (θ ι ↦ (tval_gr ϰ ι (⧺ ρ (∷ (ϰ (nthu_gr ρ (◀ θ)) (◀ (▶ θ))) ⊥)))) ρ)
⍝ ---- isomorphism by search: images τ of the generators (of the same orders); the induced map along the tree must respect every
⍝ edge (then it is a homomorphism) and be injective
hm_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹))) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹))) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔹
hm_gr ε ϑ τ ι ≔ ((ρ ↦ (∧ (∀ₗ (υ ↦ (equp_gr (comp_gr (nthu_gr ρ (◀ υ)) (nthu_gr τ (◀ (▶ υ)))) (nthu_gr ρ (▶ (▶ υ))))) ε) (equ_gr (lenu_gr (usort_gr cmpp_gr ρ)) (lenu_gr ρ)))) (tval_gr (μ κ ↦ (comp_gr μ (nthu_gr τ κ))) ϑ (∷ ι ⊥)))
⍝ the candidate images: τ₁ one representative per conjugacy class of H (composing with an inner automorphism of H moves any
⍝ image of s₁ to its class representative), then each τⱼ of the order of sⱼ with ord(τᵢ τⱼ) = ord(sᵢ sⱼ) for every i < j
eql_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹) → 𝔹
eql_gr ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (∧ (equ_gr θ θ′) (eql_gr ι ι′))) ⊥)) (∅ η))
reqs′_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))
reqs′_gr ξ ρ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (∷ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (ordu_gr (comp_gr ζ θ))) ρ) (reqs′_gr ι (⧺ ρ (∷ θ ⊥))))) ⊥)
tups_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹))) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))
tups_gr ξ η ≔ (foldl (ρ τ ↦ (concat (⫶ (ω ↦ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⧺ ω (∷ ζ ⊥))) (filter (ζ ↦ (eql_gr (⫶ (υ ↦ (ordu_gr (comp_gr υ ζ))) ω) (▶ τ))) (◀ τ)))) ρ))) (∷ ⊥ ⊥) (zw_gr ⊗ ξ η))
cands_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)))
cands_gr ς η ≔ ((ω ↦ (ς (θ ι ↦ (∷ (filter (ζ ↦ (equ_gr (ordu_gr ζ) (ordu_gr θ))) (⫶ hd (ccl_gr η))) (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⫶ ▶ (filter (υ ↦ (equ_gr (◀ υ) (ordu_gr ζ))) ω))) ι))) ⊥)) (⫶ (θ ↦ (⊗ (ordu_gr θ) θ)) η))
iso_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
iso_gr ξ η ≔ ((ς ↦ ((ν ↦ ((ε ↦ ((ϑ ↦ (∃ₗ (τ ↦ (hm_gr ε ϑ τ (iotau_gr (degs_gr η)))) (tups_gr (cands_gr ς η) (reqs′_gr ς ⊥)))) (tre_gr ν ε))) (edg_gr ν ς))) (bfsn_gr ς (iotau_gr (degs_gr ξ))))) (ggen_gr ξ))
⍝ ---- abelian invariants: G/G′ ≅ ℤᵏ / L, k generators, L spanned by the edge relations coord(y) + e_s − coord(y∘s) of the
⍝ Cayley graph (the Schreier generators of the relation module); the invariant factors come from a Smith normal form of them
zw_gr ∶ (α → β → γ) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 β → 𝔏 γ
zw_gr ϰ ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (∷ (ϰ θ θ′) (zw_gr ϰ ι ι′))) ⊥)) ⊥)
uvec_gr ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔇
uvec_gr ς κ ≔ (⫶ (τ ↦ ((equ_gr (▶ τ) κ) (◀ 1) ⊥)) (wix_gr ς))
⍝ the Smith normal form works on digit strings 𝔇 (real integers): ∅ᶻ ⊟ᶻ ⊠ᶻ ⌊ᶻ, no fractions
nzr_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔹
nzr_gr ξ ≔ (∃ₗ (θ ↦ (¬ (∅ᶻ θ))) ξ)
⍝ the better pivot row: nonzero head, smallest in absolute value; a row with a positive head (negated if needed)
bpv_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
bpv_gr ξ η ≔ ((∅ᶻ (hd ξ)) η ((∅ᶻ (hd η)) ξ (((⋚ʳ (⊟ᶻ (absᶻ (hd η)) (absᶻ (hd ξ)))) ⊤ ⊥ ⊥) η ξ)))
posr_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
posr_gr ξ ≔ (((⋚ʳ (hd ξ)) ⊤ ⊥ ⊥) (⫶ ⊖ᶻ ξ) ξ)
⍝ a row minus ⌊head / pivot⌋ times the pivot row (pivot > 0): its head becomes its remainder, 0 ≤ head < pivot
redr_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
redr_gr ξ ρ ≔ ((θ ↦ (zw_gr (μ ν ↦ (⊟ᶻ μ (⊠ᶻ θ ν))) ξ ρ)) (⌊ᶻ (hd ξ) (hd ρ)))
⍝ the position (unary, from 1) of the first nonzero entry; a row with its entries 0 and κ exchanged (a column swap)
fnz_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
fnz_gr ξ κ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ ((∅ᶻ θ) (fnz_gr ι (∷ ⊤ κ)) κ)) κ)
swp_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔇
swp_gr ξ κ ≔ ((μ ν ↦ (⫶ (τ ↦ ((∅ (▶ τ)) ν ((equ_gr (▶ τ) κ) μ (◀ τ)))) (wix_gr ξ))) (hd ξ) (nthu_gr ξ κ))
⍝ a diagonal form of an integer matrix (list of rows): eliminate column 0 below the pivot of least absolute value (Euclid on the
⍝ rows); then reduce the pivot row modulo the pivot (column operations that touch only that row); if a remainder is left, swap that
⍝ column in front (the pivot strictly decreases), else the pivot is a diagonal entry and the rest is done recursively
snf_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔇) → 𝔏 𝔇
snf_gr μ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((∅ σ) ⊥ ((∀ₗ (ξ ↦ (∅ᶻ (hd ξ))) σ) (∷ ⊥ (snf_gr (⫶ ⌄ σ))) ((ρ ↦ ((τ ↦ ((∀ₗ (ξ ↦ (∅ᶻ (hd ξ))) τ) (snp_gr ρ τ) (snf_gr (∷ ρ τ)))) (filter nzr_gr (⫶ (ξ ↦ (redr_gr ξ ρ)) σ)))) (posr_gr (foldl bpv_gr (hd σ) (⌄ σ))))))) (filter nzr_gr μ))
snp_gr ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 (𝔏 𝔇) → 𝔏 𝔇
snp_gr ρ τ ≔ ((θ ↦ ((ω ↦ ((∀ₗ ∅ᶻ ω) (∷ θ (snf_gr (⫶ ⌄ τ))) ((κ ↦ (snf_gr (⫶ (ξ ↦ (swp_gr ξ κ)) (∷ (∷ θ ω) τ)))) (fnz_gr ω (∷ ⊤ ⊥))))) (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⊟ᶻ ζ (⊠ᶻ θ (⌊ᶻ ζ θ)))) (⌄ ρ)))) (hd ρ))
⍝ ℤ/a × ℤ/l₁ × … × ℤ/lₘ (l₁ | … | lₘ) as a divisibility chain: (gcd, lcm) passed along
ins_gr ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
ins_gr μ ξ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (∷ (gcd μ θ) (ins_gr (lcm μ θ) ι))) (∷ μ ⊥))
abinv_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 ℕ
abinv_gr ξ ≔ ((ς ↦ ((ν ↦ ((ε ↦ ((ρ ↦ (filter (ζ ↦ (¬ (≐ ζ 1))) (foldr ins_gr ⊥ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⊗ ζ (◀ 1))) (snf_gr (⫶ (υ ↦ (zw_gr ⊟ᶻ (zw_gr ⊞ᶻ (nthu_gr ρ (◀ υ)) (uvec_gr ς (◀ (▶ υ)))) (nthu_gr ρ (▶ (▶ υ))))) ε)))))) (tval_gr (μ κ ↦ (zw_gr ⊞ᶻ μ (uvec_gr ς κ))) (tre_gr ν ε) (∷ (⫶ (θ ↦ ⊥) ς) ⊥)))) (edg_gr ν ς))) (bfsn_gr ς (iotau_gr (degs_gr ξ))))) (ggen_gr ξ))
⍝ colourings of the points with κ colours up to the group: (1/|G|) Σ κ^(number of cycles of g)
colr_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → ℕ → ℕ
colr_gr ξ κ ≔ (⊜ (div (sumof (⫶ (θ ↦ (^ κ (n_gr (lenu_gr (lens_gr θ))))) ξ)) (ℓ ξ)))
⍝ ---- public: finite groups (a group is the sorted list of its elements; lists are padded to one degree, sorted, without repetitions)
grouporder ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ      ⍝ the order |G|: the number of distinct elements of the list
grouporder ξ ≔ (ℓ (ing_gr ξ))
isgroup ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔹      ⍝ is the list a group: non-empty, permutations (padded to one degree), closed under composition?
isgroup ξ ≔ (grp_gr (ing_gr ξ))
issubgroup ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔹      ⍝ is H a subgroup of G (G a group, H ⊆ G non-empty and closed)?
issubgroup η ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ (∧ (grp_gr (▶ σ)) (sgp_gr (◀ σ) (▶ σ)))) (ing2_gr η ξ))
isnormal ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔹      ⍝ is H a normal subgroup of the group G (g H g⁻¹ = H for every g ∈ G)?
isnormal η ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ (∧ (∧ (grp_gr (▶ σ)) (sgp_gr (◀ σ) (▶ σ))) (equ_gr (lenu_gr (norm_gr (◀ σ) (▶ σ))) (lenu_gr (▶ σ))))) (ing2_gr η ξ))
leftcosets ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ))      ⍝ the left cosets gH of the subgroup H in G, each sorted, in order of their least element; [] unless H is a subgroup of the group G
leftcosets η ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((∧ (grp_gr (▶ σ)) (sgp_gr (◀ σ) (▶ σ))) (⫶ outg_gr (cos′_gr comp_gr (◀ σ) (▶ σ))) ⊥)) (ing2_gr η ξ))
rightcosets ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ))      ⍝ the right cosets Hg of the subgroup H in G, each sorted, in order of their least element; [] unless H is a subgroup of the group G
rightcosets η ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((∧ (grp_gr (▶ σ)) (sgp_gr (◀ σ) (▶ σ))) (⫶ outg_gr (cos′_gr (θ ζ ↦ (comp_gr ζ θ)) (◀ σ) (▶ σ))) ⊥)) (ing2_gr η ξ))
index ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ      ⍝ the index [G : H] = |G| / |H| of the subgroup H; 0 unless H is a subgroup of the group G
index η ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((∧ (grp_gr (▶ σ)) (sgp_gr (◀ σ) (▶ σ))) (⊜ (div (ℓ (▶ σ)) (ℓ (◀ σ)))) 0)) (ing2_gr η ξ))
conjclasses ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ))      ⍝ the conjugacy classes {x g x⁻¹} of the group G, each sorted, in order of their least element; [] unless G is a group
conjclasses ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) (⫶ outg_gr (ccl_gr σ)) ⊥)) (ing_gr ξ))
center ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the centre Z(G): the elements that commute with every element (sorted)
center ξ ≔ (outg_gr (cent_gr (ing_gr ξ)))
centralizer ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the centralizer C_G(x): the elements of G that commute with x (sorted; x and G padded to one degree)
centralizer ζ ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((θ ↦ (outg_gr (filter (υ ↦ (equp_gr (comp_gr υ θ) (comp_gr θ υ))) (▶ σ)))) (hd (◀ σ)))) (ing2_gr (∷ ζ ⊥) ξ))
normalizer ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the normalizer N_G(H): the elements g of G with g H g⁻¹ = H (H any set of permutations; sorted)
normalizer η ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ (outg_gr (norm_gr (◀ σ) (▶ σ)))) (ing2_gr η ξ))
commutatorsubgroup ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the derived subgroup G′ = [G, G], generated by the commutators a b a⁻¹ b⁻¹ (sorted); [] unless G is a group
commutatorsubgroup ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) (outg_gr (comm_gr σ)) ⊥)) (ing_gr ξ))
issolvable ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔹      ⍝ is the group solvable (its derived series G ⊇ G′ ⊇ G″ ⊇ … reaches the trivial group)? ⊥ unless G is a group
issolvable ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ (∧ (grp_gr σ) (solv_gr σ))) (ing_gr ξ))
isabelian ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔹      ⍝ is G an abelian group (a b = b a for all elements)? ⊥ unless G is a group
isabelian ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ (∧ (grp_gr σ) (abel_gr σ))) (ing_gr ξ))
iscyclic ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔹      ⍝ is G a cyclic group (it has an element of order |G|)? ⊥ unless G is a group
iscyclic ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ (∧ (grp_gr σ) (cycl_gr σ))) (ing_gr ξ))
elementorders ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔓 ℕ ℕ)      ⍝ the element-order statistics: the pairs (order, number of elements of that order), by increasing order; [] unless G is a group
elementorders ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) (⫶ (τ ↦ (⊗ (n_gr (◀ τ)) (n_gr (▶ τ)))) (eord_gr σ)) ⊥)) (ing_gr ξ))
exponent ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ      ⍝ the exponent of G: the lcm of the orders of its elements; 0 unless G is a group
exponent ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) (n_gr (foldl lcmu_gr (∷ ⊤ ⊥) (⫶ ordu_gr σ))) 0)) (ing_gr ξ))
orbit ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the orbit of the point i under the group generated by the list (a group or generators), sorted; [i] for a point beyond the degree
orbit ξ κ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((ν ↦ ((equ_gr ν (degs_gr σ)) (∷ κ ⊥) (⫶ n_gr (orb_gr σ ν)))) (uc_gr κ (degs_gr σ)))) (inl_gr ξ))
orbits ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the orbits on 0 … n − 1 (n the degree) of the group generated by the list, each sorted, in order of their least point
orbits ξ ≔ (⫶ (⫶ n_gr) (orbs_gr (inl_gr ξ)))
stabilizer ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the stabilizer of the point i: the elements g with g(i) = i (sorted; all of G for a point beyond the degree)
stabilizer ξ κ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((ν ↦ (outg_gr ((equ_gr ν (degs_gr σ)) σ (filter (θ ↦ (equ_gr (ap_gr θ ν) ν)) σ)))) (uc_gr κ (degs_gr σ)))) (ing_gr ξ))
burnside ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ      ⍝ the number of orbits of the group on its points 0 … n − 1, by Burnside's lemma (the mean number of fixed points); 0 unless G is a group
burnside ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) (n_gr (burn_gr σ)) 0)) (ing_gr ξ))
cayleytable ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the Cayley table: entry (i, j) is the position k of gᵢ∘gⱼ = g_k in the sorted element list; [] unless G is a group
cayleytable ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((ρ ↦ ((∧ (∀ₗ permi_gr σ) (∀ₗ ◀ ρ)) (⫶ (υ ↦ (⫶ n_gr (▶ υ))) ρ) ⊥)) (⫶ (crow_gr σ) σ))) (ing_gr ξ))
directproduct ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the direct product G × H acting on disjoint points: (g, h) acts as g on 0 … n − 1 and as h on n, n + 1, … (sorted)
directproduct ξ η ≔ (outg_gr (dprod_gr (ing_gr ξ) (ing_gr η)))
sylow ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ a Sylow p-subgroup of G (order the largest power of p dividing |G|; sorted), grown inside normalizers; the trivial subgroup when p is not a prime or does not divide |G|; [] unless G is a group
sylow ξ κ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) ((ν ↦ ((primeu_gr ν) (outg_gr (syl_gr σ ν)) (outg_gr (∷ (iotau_gr (degs_gr σ)) ⊥)))) (uc_gr κ (∷ ⊤ σ))) ⊥)) (ing_gr ξ))
subgroups ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ))      ⍝ all subgroups of G, by increasing order then lexicographically (cyclic subgroups joined until closure; small groups: S₄ ~3 s, order 48 ~1 min); [] unless G is a group
subgroups ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) (⫶ outg_gr (usort_gr cmpo_gr (sgrs_gr σ))) ⊥)) (ing_gr ξ))
sinv_gr ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔏 (𝔏 (𝔏 𝔹)) → 𝔹
sinv_gr σ τ ≔ (∧ (equ_gr (lenu_gr σ) (lenu_gr τ)) (∧ (eqo_gr (eord_gr σ) (eord_gr τ)) (∧ (equ_gr (lenu_gr (cent_gr σ)) (lenu_gr (cent_gr τ))) (∧ (¬ (⊻ (abel_gr σ) (abel_gr τ))) (∧ (¬ (⊻ (cycl_gr σ) (cycl_gr τ))) (¬ (⊻ (solv_gr σ) (solv_gr τ))))))))
sameinvariants ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔹      ⍝ do the groups agree in order, element-order statistics, centre size, and being abelian, cyclic, solvable? A necessary condition for isomorphism, NOT a proof of it (⊥ unless both are groups)
sameinvariants ξ η ≔ ((σ τ ↦ (∧ (∧ (grp_gr σ) (grp_gr τ)) (sinv_gr σ τ))) (ing_gr ξ) (ing_gr η))
isomorphic ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔹      ⍝ are the groups isomorphic? A real test: images of a generating list of G (same orders) are searched for a map that respects every edge of the Cayley graph and is injective; exponential in the number of generators (small groups, order ≲ 32)
isomorphic ξ η ≔ ((σ τ ↦ (∧ (∧ (grp_gr σ) (grp_gr τ)) (∧ (equ_gr (lenu_gr σ) (lenu_gr τ)) (∧ (eqo_gr (eord_gr σ) (eord_gr τ)) (iso_gr σ τ))))) (ing_gr ξ) (ing_gr η))
abelianinvariants ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the invariant factors d₁ | d₂ | … (all > 1) of the abelianization G/G′ ≅ ℤ/d₁ × ℤ/d₂ × … (of G itself when G is abelian), by a Smith normal form of the Cayley-graph relations; [] for a perfect group or a list that is not a group
abelianinvariants ξ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) (⫶ ⊜ (abinv_gr σ)) ⊥)) (ing_gr ξ))
colorings ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the number of colourings of the n points with k colours up to the group (orbits on the kⁿ colourings, by Burnside: the mean of k^(number of cycles)); 0 unless G is a group
colorings ξ κ ≔ ((σ ↦ ((grp_gr σ) (colr_gr σ κ) 0)) (ing_gr ξ))
necklaces ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the number of necklaces of n beads in k colours (colourings up to rotation)
necklaces ν κ ≔ (colr_gr (cycz_gr (u_gr ν)) κ)
bracelets ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the number of bracelets of n beads in k colours (colourings up to rotation and reflection)
bracelets ν κ ≔ (colr_gr (dih_gr (u_gr ν)) κ)
semidirect ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the semidirect product ℤ/m ⋊ ℤ/n, the generator of ℤ/n acting by x ↦ a x, as its regular permutation group on m n points ((b, j) is the point b + m j, (b, j)(b′, j′) = (b + aʲ b′, j + j′)); [] unless m, n ≥ 1, gcd(a, m) = 1 and aⁿ ≡ 1 (mod m)
semidirect μ ν κ ≔ ((∧ (≻ μ 0) (∧ (≻ ν 0) (∧ (≐ (gcd κ μ) 1) (≐ (foldl (ρ θ ↦ (mod (⊠ ρ κ) μ)) (mod 1 μ) (⍳ ν)) (mod 1 μ))))) (generate (∷ (concat (⫶ (ι ↦ (⫶ (θ ↦ (⊜ (⊞ (mod (⊞ θ 1) μ) (⊠ μ ι)))) (⍳ μ))) (⍳ ν))) (∷ (concat (⫶ (ι ↦ (⫶ (θ ↦ (⊜ (⊞ (mod (⊠ κ θ) μ) (⊠ μ (mod (⊞ ι 1) ν))))) (⍳ μ))) (⍳ ν))) ⊥))) ⊥)
